# Language and path rules

- Reply to the user in **English only**. Do not use Chinese in chat, commits, comments, or project files.
- All new or edited project text must be English: Markdown, YAML/JSON comments, Java/JS comments, OpenAPI descriptions, commit messages.
- Do not leave leftover Chinese in files you touch. Translate it; do not delete meaning.

## Markdown paths

Never write a machine-specific absolute path in `*.md`:

- Bad: `d:\常用文件\...`, `C:\Users\...`, `/Users/...`, `/home/...`
- Good: repo-relative paths such as `design/SCOPE-BASELINE.md`, `dealer-core/src/main/resources/db/migration/V1__init.sql`

Use GitHub URLs or env-var placeholders (`$JAVA_HOME`, sibling checkout named `ai-manager`) instead of a local disk layout.

```md
<!-- BAD -->
Source: `D:\常用文件\SAIT\26fall\Capstone\Project Topics\DealerOps`

<!-- GOOD -->
Source: `design/IMPLEMENTATION-BRIEF.md` in this repository
```
